  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote `src/main.ts`: a procedural desert canyon at dusk with a looping camera flythrough on the `#app` canvas. `typecheck` passes. I could not run it, build it with `vite build`, or look at a frame, so lighting brightness, shadow quality, fog density and sky colours are untested guesses.\n\n- **Terrain:** one heightfield mesh (about 37k vertices) follows a winding centre line. It has a dry riverbed channel and steep, terraced sandstone walls on both sides. Vertex colours give the strata bands, dusty ledges and darkening near the wall bases. The terrain repeats every 240 m, so the camera loop has no seam.\n- **Props:** instanced rounded boulders and blocks are placed away from the camera path. Dead shrubs are small clumps with stick branches.\n- **Lighting and sky:**\n  - The sky is a gradient from orange at the horizon through magenta to blue-violet overhead, with a low sun.\n  - A warm directional sun at 13° elevation casts cascaded shadows. A cool fill light and a violet-and-warm hemisphere light add ambient.\n  - Distance fog in a mauve tone fades far walls toward the sky, and a mild bloom softens the sun.\n- **Camera:** it moves at about 5.5 m/s (a loop of roughly 44 s) at about 1.75 m height, swaying left and right with a slight roll and a look-ahead target. It is updated every frame with `app.camera.setPose`.\n- **Contract:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set after two `requestAnimationFrame` callbacks, which follow `app.ready()`. The engine's own render loop draws continuously.\n- **No external assets:** nothing is loaded from the network.\n\n",
